the default plan is untiled: a Grid over the rows and a workgroup over the columns: true
untiled: the operands' requested bytes are at least M*N*K*elt: true
untiled: the operands' requested bytes are at most M*N*K*elt*(1 + 1/wg): true
every scalar blocktile requests exactly M*N*K*elt*(1/bm + 1/bn) of its operands: true
the untiled plan's working set is positive: true
with no capacity the score is analyze's roofline: true
at capacity (working set = capacity) the score is analyze's roofline: true
past capacity the untiled score exceeds analyze's roofline: true
raising the capacity never raises the score, with or without a cache tier, on every plan: true
past capacity some scalar blocktile ranks strictly below the untiled plan: true
with no capacity no scalar blocktile ranks strictly below the untiled plan: true
the bound is at most analyze's roofline is at most the score, on every leaf: true
within capacity, the cache tier charges the untiled plan above analyze's roofline: true
within capacity, the cache tier charges less than the DRAM tier past it: true
within capacity, some scalar blocktile ranks strictly below the untiled plan: true
raising the cache bandwidth never raises the score, on every plan: true
a cache bandwidth below DRAM's is read as DRAM's: true
a 32-thread nest launched alone keeps resident / 32 of its blocks: true
beside a 256-thread sibling, it keeps only resident / 256 (the launch block's): true
a rate at or above its ceiling reads as the ceiling: the score is the one without it, on every leaf: true
raising the issue rate or the DRAM rate never raises the score, on every leaf: true
with the score's own rates, analyze's roofline under the ceilings is at most the score, on every leaf: true
under the ceilings, some scalar blocktile ranks strictly below the untiled plan: true
an issue rate with the ceiling's DRAM leaves no scalar blocktile strictly below the untiled plan: true
with both rates, some scalar blocktile ranks strictly below the untiled plan: true
every leaf's memory leg is at least its global nodes' distinct bytes, writes included, at the DRAM rate: true
the reuse extraction lists exactly the nodes no global placement holds: true
a staged blocktile's tiles are off the DRAM leg: its memory leg is below the same extraction charging them: true
an all-accepted-tile-MMA kernel's compute leg does not depend on the issue rate: true
with no accepted tile-MMA work, the compute leg is all operations at the issue rate: true
an accepted count above the operations reads as the operations: true
a tile-MMA rate prices exactly the accepted work: the rest at the issue rate, it at its own: true
a tile-MMA rate alone, at the issue ceiling, still prices the accepted work at its own rate: true
a tile-MMA rate above the ceiling reads as the ceiling: true
device gathers without a gather rate leave the compute leg as it was: true
device gathers add exactly their count over the gather rate: true
at the ceilings, device gathers add their count over the gather rate to the bound's quotient: true
a gather rate without gathers adds nothing: true
the tile-MMA rate and the gathers leave the memory leg unchanged: true
with every rate set, the compute leg is at least the bound's: true
the staffed start's gate tag tells two issue rates apart: true
the staffed start's gate tag tells two DRAM rates apart: true
the staffed start's gate tag tells two tile-MMA rates apart: true
the staffed start's gate tag tells two device-gather rates apart: true
the staffed start's gate tag tells two memory-transaction rates apart: true
serial: with no capacity a one-block nest requests its distinct bytes: true
serial: at capacity (the nest's bytes) it requests its distinct bytes: true
serial: past capacity, where every loop's iteration fits, it requests its distinct bytes: true
serial: past an o-iteration, x is re-read once per o; dy and dw are kept: true
serial: past an i-iteration, dy is re-read once per i as well: true
serial: past a k-iteration, the accumulator is re-read once per k as well: true
serial: the loop interchange (i, o, k) moves the re-read from x to dy: true
serial: a read every loop indexes is never re-read: true
serial: past an o-iteration the score charges x's re-reads: true
serial: the score with no capacity is analyze's distinct bytes: true
serial: raising the capacity never raises the score: true
serial: completion_floor <= analyze <= the score, at every capacity: true
a Grid plan's requested bytes do not depend on the serial re-read charge: true
